diff --git a/audits/2026-11-02-v0.5.0-cochilo.md b/audits/2026-11-02-v0.5.0-cochilo.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d8bbcc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/audits/2026-11-02-v0.5.0-cochilo.md
@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@
+# Audit: Cochilo joins the system (0.4.0)
+
+Date: 2026-11-01 · PR: Cochilo layer (see CHANGELOG 0.4.0) · Auditor: Claude Code, with both required skills
+
+- **graphic-design-fundamentals**: `SKILL.md` §13 read from `.claude/skills/` and applied by hand
+  (the session runs outside this repo, so the skill was not auto-loaded).
+- **impeccable** 4.8.0: `reference/audit.native.md` scored against `reference/android.md`, applied
+  by hand; the launcher was not run. `critique` applied to the screenshots below.
+
+## Scope
+
+Added, nothing existing changed in value (uikit and PulseLoop generated files only get the new
+version in their header line):
+
+- Layer `cochilo` (Compose, light + dark): all 10 core colours; `panel` `#17161A`/`#000000`,
+  `on-panel`, `on-panel-muted` (same values as uikit); `snackbar` = `{ink}`;
+  `snackbar-action` `#43F3B7` / `#0A7A55` (uikit's values, marked `pair`); **new** data hues `event-night` `#5B4BDB`/`#9A8CFF`,
+  `event-nap` `#1C7ED6`/`#5BA8FF`, `event-feed` `#C2570C`/`#FF9A5C`, `event-pump` `#8E44C9`/`#C98CFF`,
+  `event-diaper` `#B8407A`/`#FF7FA8`, `event-daylight` `#8C6A00`/`#FFD25C`; uikit's type roles,
+  spacing and radii; sizes `header` 56, `tabbar` 64, `button` 52, `monogram` 32, `row-min` 56,
+  **new** `timeline` 24; core motion.
+- Contrast: 12 existing pairs extended to `cochilo` (including `snackbar-action` on `snackbar`);
+  12 new pairs (each event hue on `page` and `surface` at 3:1). `panel`, `on-panel` and
+  `snackbar-action` are marked `pair` (they share a light value with ink, surface and mint).
+- Fairy mode is not carried: its trigger is the profile name, and Cochilo's profile is the baby
+  (D-11). `check_variants` therefore has nothing to require of this layer.
+- Generator `generated/cochilo/CTokens.kt` + `generated/web/cochilo.css`; `drift.py --cochilo`; a test.
+- Assets: `CO_` mark; `gg_ic_chart`, `gg_ic_moon`, `gg_ic_sun` in the existing line style (Lucide
+  geometry, 24 viewport, 22dp, stroke 1.75, round caps and joins).
+- Docs: apps tables, PRODUCT, consuming, tokens, foundations (data palette), components (Sleep panel,
+  Timeline / actogram), divergence D-11.
+
+The first consumer, the Cochilo app (gabrielbr/Cochilo), was audited with it, because a token is only
+as good as the place it is used.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals (§13 checklist)
+
+| # | Question | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | ✅ A night-time, one-handed baby log that predicts the next nap. The layer gives it the family look plus what it needs that others don't: event data hues and a dark sleep panel. |
+| 2 | Concept | ✅ Same concept as the family: mono type, mint frame, one accent. The sleep panel going dark while the baby sleeps is the one app-specific idea, and it serves the brief (less light at night). |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | ✅ Today reads: state + timer (timer role) → the one mint action → next nap (title role) → log. Squint test passes in both themes (screenshots). |
+| 4 | Contrast | ✅ All text pairs ≥ 4.5:1, all event hues ≥ 3:1 on page and surface in both themes (Evidence). ⚠️ C-1: night vs nap hues are close to each other. |
+| 5 | Alignment and grid | ✅ Single column, 24dp gutter (32 from 600dp), captions and groups on one left edge; actogram labels in a fixed column so bars align. |
+| 6 | Spacing | ✅ Only the core scale; 40 above captions, 12 below; groups separated by space, rows by hairlines. |
+| 7 | Typography | ✅ One family; uikit's roles reused (no new role names, so D-1 doesn't grow). 12sp floor kept (caption, chips, tab labels). |
+| 8 | Colour | ✅ Mint only for the one action, the title highlighter, the active tab and the frame; "due" chip is mint because it means "act now". Event hues only on data and always next to a word (legend, row label, spoken summary). Works in grayscale through position and labels. |
+| 9 | Consistency | ✅ Components follow docs/components.md (header, tab bar, row group, buttons, chips, sheet, snackbar). Two new components documented. |
+| 10 | Simplicity | ✅ Six data hues for six event types, nothing decorative. One thing that could go: the plus icon on every log button (kept: it says "add" to a tired reader; see C-8). |
+| 11 | Real-size test | 🟡 Paparazzi renders at Pixel 5 size, light/dark, EN/PT (below). No emulator in this session (no KVM), so a device pass is still open (C-7). |
+| 12 | Accessibility and ergonomics | ✅ 48dp targets, 56dp rows, filter pills inside 48dp areas, TalkBack labels, live timer, spoken timeline summaries, Remove animations honoured. ⚠️ C-6. |
+| 13 | Production | ✅ Generated Kotlin, bundled Ubuntu Mono with licence, vector icons, launcher icon drawn from the font's own glyphs. ⚠️ C-3. |
+
+Issues by severity: **critical** none; **important** C-1, C-2 (owner decision), C-4, C-5;
+**polish** C-3, C-6, C-7, C-8.
+
+## impeccable (audit, native / Android) — Cochilo 0.1.0 on the new layer
+
+| # | Dimension | Score | Key finding |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Accessibility | 3 | Labels, live regions, spoken chart summaries and targets in place; not yet verified with TalkBack on a device or at 200% font (C-7) |
+| 2 | Performance | 3 | History draws up to 60 days in a scrolling Column, not a LazyColumn (C-4) |
+| 3 | Appearance & theming | 4 | Every colour, size, radius and duration comes from `CTokens`; Material roles mapped from the tokens; dark is designed |
+| 4 | Platform conformance | 3 | Edge-to-edge with insets, system Back, Material sheets, pickers and snackbar; the family's own buttons and tab bar by design |
+| 5 | Adaptivity | 2 | Gutter widens at 600dp, but no navigation rail or content cap on tablets (C-5) |
+| | **Total** | **15/20** | **Good** |
+
+**Platform conformance verdict:** passes. It reads as a native Android app themed by the family
+system: bottom navigation with three destinations, system Back works everywhere (Settings is a
+pushed screen), bottom sheets for entry and confirmation, snackbar with Undo for deletion.
+
+### Findings
+
+- **[P2] C-1 Night and nap hues are close** (`event-night`/`event-nap` 1.44:1 light, 1.12:1 dark).
+  Location: timeline, actogram. Impact: someone who can't tell indigo from blue relies on position
+  (night sleep sits at the ends of the bar) and the labelled list. Guideline: WCAG 1.4.1 (not colour
+  alone) is met through labels; distinguishing the two at a glance is nicer. Recommendation: keep,
+  or give naps a hatch/dither in a later version. `/impeccable colorize`.
+- **[P2] C-2 Night viewing (D-11).** The 4dp mint frame and the mint button stay bright at 3am.
+  Research favours dim, warm or red light at night. Changing the frame touches a brand commitment, so
+  it is recorded as D-11 for the owner, not changed here.
+- **[P2] C-4 History is not virtualised.** `ui/screens/HistoryPatterns.kt`: up to 60 days of
+  timelines and rows in a `verticalScroll` Column. Fine for weeks, heavy after months.
+  Recommendation: `LazyColumn` with day items. `/impeccable optimize`.
+- **[P2] C-5 No tablet layout.** Recommendation: navigation rail and 720dp content cap from 600dp,
+  as PulseLoop does. `/impeccable adapt`.
+- **[P3] C-3 Window background duplicates two tokens.** `res/values*/colors.xml` holds `page` and
+  `panel` as hex for the pre-Compose window and launcher. Recommendation: have `gen_tokens.py` also
+  emit a `colors.xml` for this layer.
+- **[P3] C-6 Remove animations is read once** at composition start, so changing it needs an app
+  restart. `/impeccable animate`.
+- **[P3] C-7 No device pass yet** (TalkBack, 200% font, gestures). Do it on the Pixel before 1.0.
+- **[P3] C-8 Plus icon on every log button** repeats; consider dropping it once the buttons are known.
+
+### Positive findings
+
+- The app copies `generated/cochilo/CTokens.kt` byte for byte: `drift.py --cochilo` reports 0.
+- `snackbar-action` passes in both themes (12.6:1 / 4.8:1); the app's snackbar uses it from day one.
+- The sleep panel uses the existing `panel` colours: no new pair, and the screen gets darker, not
+  brighter, while the baby sleeps.
+- Data hues are used only on data and always with a word; every chart has a spoken summary.
+
+## Evidence
+
+```
+$ python3 scripts/check_tokens.py
+check-tokens: 0 error(s), 0 tracked warning(s)
+
+$ python3 scripts/drift.py --pulseloop ../PulseLoopAndroid --cochilo ../Cochilo
+drift: 0 difference(s)
+
+$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests
+OK
+```
+
+NotTheOmiAIApp was not checked out in this session; its generated file changed only in the header
+line, which `drift.py` ignores.
+
+Event hues, contrast on surface / page:
+
+| Token | Light | Dark |
+|---|---|---|
+| event-night | 6.04 / 5.40 | 6.17 / 6.74 |
+| event-nap | 4.20 / 3.75 | 6.93 / 7.56 |
+| event-feed | 4.50 / 4.02 | 8.18 / 8.94 |
+| event-pump | 5.50 / 4.91 | 7.08 / 7.73 |
+| event-diaper | 5.18 / 4.63 | 7.22 / 7.89 |
+| event-daylight | 5.03 / 4.49 | 11.93 / 13.03 |
+| snackbar-action on snackbar (text) | 12.64 | 4.78 |
+
+Screenshots (Paparazzi, Pixel 5): `Cochilo/app/src/test/snapshots/images/` — Today light, dark,
+sleeping (dark), pt-BR; History; Patterns light, dark, pt-BR dark; Settings; empty Today.
+
+## Verdict
+
+Merge: no critical, P0 or P1 findings introduced. Open, carried forward: C-2 (= D-11, owner
+decision), C-1, C-4, C-5, then C-3, C-6, C-7, C-8.
