+# Brands
+
+A **brand** dresses an app as a partner's product without taking it out of the system. Cochilo is
+the first: it ships as **Cochilo, da Tatá Slings**, a product of Tatá's babywearing shop.
+
+Status: ✅ `brands.tata-slings`, worn by the `cochilo` layer (0.6.0).
+
+## What a brand changes, and what it never does
+
+| A brand swaps | A brand never touches |
+|---|---|
+| The app's colour roles: `page`, `surface`, `ink`, `muted`, `line`, the brand accent (`mint` role), `on-mint`, the alert roles, panel and snackbar colours | Spacing, radii, sizes, motion, the type scale (sizes, line heights, weights per role) |
+| The one type family (and its faces) | Data colours (`event-*`, `metric-*`, `stage-*`, `zone-*`): their meaning is the system's |
+| The app's mark (an asset in `assets/logos/`) | Components, icons, the frame, the targets, copy rules, the update flow |
+| | Any rule in AGENTS.md: one filled accent action per screen, contrast, 48dp, tokens only… |
+
+So a branded app still reads like a Gabriel app (same rhythm, same components, same behaviour) and
+looks like the partner's product (their colours, their typeface, their mark).
+
+The role names stay. Under a brand, `mint` means "the brand accent": the one filled action, the
+frame, the active tab, the title highlighter. Keeping the names means no app code changes when a
+brand is put on or taken off; only the generated values move.
+
+## How it's built
+
+- `tokens.json` → `brands.<key>`: `name`, `doc`, `source` (where the values were measured), `type`
+  (`family`, `faces`, `licence`) and `color`, a list of `{replaces, value: {light, dark}, usage}`.
+- A layer opts in with `"brand": "<key>"`.
+- `tokens_lib.colour_map` applies the brand after aliases are followed, so the generator, the
+  contrast check and `drift.py` all see the app as it ships.
+- The generated `CTokens.kt` gains `object Brand { key, name, fontFamily }`; each replaced colour's
+  comment starts with the brand's name. The CSS sets `--gds-font` to the brand's family.
+- `check_tokens.py` (`check_brands`): a brand may only replace colours the layer has, never a data
+  colour, needs a value for every theme the layer ships, names its family and faces, and carries
+  nothing else (no spacing, radius, size…). Every contrast pair is re-checked with the brand on.
+
+## Tatá Slings
+
+Measured from tataslings.com.br on 2026-11-02 (its theme CSS and logo): teal `#5DC2BB` on the
+logo and buttons, navy `#13293D` as the accent, Libre Franklin across the site. The warm neutrals
+take her fabric names (Pérola, Cereja). Full brand study, voice and rationale: the Cochilo repo,
+`docs/tata-slings/`.
+
+| Role | Light | Dark | Contrast that matters |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| page | `#FBF7F2` Pérola | `#10161C` | |
+| surface | `#FFFFFF` | `#171D24` | |
+| ink | `#13293D` navy | `#EDF1F4` | 13.9:1 / 16.0:1 on page |
+| muted | `#5F6B78` | `#A3B0BC` | 5.1:1 / 8.2:1 on page |
+| line | `#E9E2D8` | `#26303A` | never text |
+| mint (brand accent) | `#5DC2BB` teal | `#5DC2BB` | fill only: 2.1:1 on white, so never text |
+| on-mint | `#13293D` | `#10161C` | 7.0:1 / 8.6:1 |
+| coral / coral-text / coral-soft | `#E07A6B` / `#B5473A` / `#FBE9E5` | `#FF9C8E` / `#FF9C8E` / `#3A2220` | coral-text 5.0:1 on page, 4.6:1 on coral-soft |
+| panel / on-panel / on-panel-muted | `#13293D` / `#FBF7F2` / `#A3B0BC` | `#0B1A27` / `#EDF1F4` / `#A3B0BC` | 13.9:1, 6.7:1 (light) |
+| snackbar / snackbar-action | `#13293D` / `#5DC2BB` | `#EDF1F4` / `#1E6E68` | 7.0:1 / 5.3:1 |
+
+Data colours stay the cochilo layer's: on Pérola they are 3.9:1 (nap) to 5.7:1 (night).
+
+**Type:** Libre Franklin 400 / 600 / 700 (`assets/fonts/libre_franklin_*.ttf`, SIL Open Font
+License 1.1, `assets/fonts/OFL-LibreFranklin.txt`). The roles' sizes and weights are the layer's;
+the timer and meta roles use tabular figures so running times don't jitter (app-side, Theme.kt).
+
+**Mark:** `assets/logos/cochilo-tata-mark.svg`: a crescent moon resting in a sling's curve, navy
+on teal. It is the launcher icon (adaptive, symbol inside the 66dp safe zone) and the header's
+32dp mark in place of the `CO_` monogram.
+
+## Adding a brand
+
+1. Measure the partner's real colours and type (their site, their print), and write the source.
+2. Add `brands.<key>`; pick values that pass every contrast pair the layer has, in every theme.
+3. Add the faces to `assets/fonts/` with their licence, and the mark to `assets/logos/`.
+4. Point the layer at it, regenerate, run `check_tokens.py` and the tests, audit, bump minor.
+5. In the app: copy the generated file, ship the faces, switch the family, swap the mark.
